CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1785383017
OL,3,CBank of England set to hold interest
OL,4,Crates at 3.75%
OL,6,FThe Office for National Statistics
OL,7,F(ONS) said earlier this week that UK
OL,8,Fconsumer price index inflation eased
OL,9,Fback to a 15-month low in June, at
OL,10,F2.6%.
OL,12,FA slowdown in food and fuel prices
OL,13,Fhelped provide an early positive
OL,14,Fsignal for new Prime Minister Andy
OL,15,FBurnham.
OL,17,FThe recent decline will have provided
OL,18,Fsome relief to the MPC, which uses
OL,19,Finterest rates as a tool to control
OL,20,Finflation.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30204
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1785383017
OL,3,CBank of England set to hold interest
OL,4,Crates at 3.75%
OL,6,FHowever, inflation is now widely
OL,7,Fexpected to swing back higher and
OL,8,Ffurther away from the Bank's 2%
OL,9,Finflation target.
OL,11,FThe Bank has previously predicted that
OL,12,Finflation will rise back to 3.25%
OL,13,Flater this year as higher energy costs
OL,14,Ffeed into household bills from July.
OL,16,FDespite this, in recent weeks
OL,17,Feconomists had largely predicted that
OL,18,Finterest rates would be kept stable at
OL,19,F3.75% for the rest of the year.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30205
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1785383017
OL,3,CBank of England set to hold interest
OL,4,Crates at 3.75%
OL,6,FBut the end of the ceasefire between
OL,7,FUS-Israeli and Iranian forces has
OL,8,Fincreased uncertainty over the
OL,9,Foutlook, amid concerns this could
OL,10,Fdrive inflation higher.
OL,12,FOil prices surged above 100 US dollars
OL,13,Fper barrel last for the first time
OL,14,Fsince May, as attacks on shipping in
OL,15,Fthe Red Sea and threats from US
OL,16,Fpresident Donald Trump pointed towards
OL,17,Fpotential supply disruption in the
OL,18,Fregion.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30206
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1785383017
OL,3,CBank of England set to hold interest
OL,4,Crates at 3.75%
OL,6,FPrices have been volatile in recent
OL,7,Fdays, sinking sharply after a fresh
OL,8,Fpause in attacks, but swung firmly
OL,9,Fhigher again on Wednesday.
OL,11,FGovernor Andrew Bailey is likely to
OL,12,Faddress how renewed hostilities have
OL,13,Finfluenced the Bank's outlook for
OL,14,Finflation and how the committee is
OL,15,Fapproaching its decisions on rates.
OL,17,FThomas Pugh, chief economist at RSM
OL,18,FUK, said he believes oil prices will
OL,19,F"largely" steer the path of interest
OL,20,Frates for the next year.
OL,26,@{D@AOU{D@IO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30207
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1785383017
OL,3,CBank of England set to hold interest
OL,4,Crates at 3.75%
OL,6,F"If they remain close to 100 dollars
OL,7,Fper barrel over the summer, a
OL,8,FSeptember rate hike would move firmly
OL,9,Fonto the table, with another in the
OL,10,Fwinter likely," he said.
OL,12,F"However, if there is another peace
OL,13,Fdeal and prices drop back a little, we
OL,14,Fthink a weakening labour market and
OL,15,Fdeteriorating economic outlook will
OL,16,Fkeep the Bank on hold this year,
OL,17,Fbefore cutting three times in 2027."
OL,26,@nD@AOUrD@OO]tD@AOUyD@dO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/8
